{"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"SessionStart","additionalContext":"Subagents: for every delegated job in this session, whether or not it belongs to a Grid task, use the Grid plugin's agents\n(subagent_type \"grid:<name>\"). Do not use general-purpose, Explore or Plan for a job one of them covers; their\n\"Grid task\" wording does not limit them to task folders. Pick by the job:\n- find where something is in the code, how a flow runs, a codebase map: grid:grid-scout\n- facts from docs, source or the web: grid:grid-researcher\n- write or change code, docs or files: grid:grid-builder\n- run a build, test, lint or read CI logs: grid:grid-runner\n- review code or finished work: grid:grid-reviewer\n- a design spec before UI is built: grid:grid-designer\n- check a page in a browser without changing it: grid:grid-checker; browser work that changes state: grid:grid-operator\n- plan a task: grid:grid-planner; write a brief: grid:grid-brief-writer; curate brain proposals: grid:grid-curator\nWith no brief, put the job in the prompt. Use general-purpose only for a job that fits none of these.\nAll Grid agents:\n- grid:grid-brief-writer: Writes one brief in a Grid task folder from the planner's ask\n- grid:grid-builder: Executes one brief in a Grid task exactly - code, UI when the brief names a design skill, docs or files - and writes its Outcome\n- grid:grid-checker: Read-only browser check for a Grid task - pages, flows, console and network errors, links, copy, screenshots against a spec - and writes its own brief's Verdict\n- grid:grid-curator: Curates a Grid task's brain proposals into finished, linked notes and writes the accepted ones into the brain\n- grid:grid-designer: Writes the design spec (spec.md) for a Grid task - layout, components, states and copy - from the project's design system\n- grid:grid-operator: Does browser work that changes state for a Grid task - forms, admin panels, dashboards, multi-page flows, uploads, saving pages to files - and writes its Outcome\n- grid:grid-planner: Plans one Grid task in its task folder\n- grid:grid-researcher: Researches one question for a Grid task from sources - the docs for the exact version a project pins, source code, papers, the web - and writes research.md or answers a worker's API question\n- grid:grid-reviewer: Reviews one finished brief in a Grid task and writes only its Verdict; with \"end review\" in the Job, reviews a whole phase\n- grid:grid-runner: Runs one command or check for a Grid task - a test, build, lint, regeneration or CI log read - and writes a short Outcome\n- grid:grid-scout: Read-only map maker for a Grid task"}}
